{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H38310","actionDate":"2026-04-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Motion to reconsider laid on the table Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H37100","actionDate":"2026-04-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"On agreeing to the resolution Agreed to by the Yeas and Nays: 219 - 207 (Roll no. 121).","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"8000","actionDate":"2026-04-16","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Passed/agreed to in House: On agreeing to the resolution Agreed to by the Yeas and Nays: 219 - 207 (Roll no. 121).","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2026-04-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H2947-2948)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"POSTPONED PROCEEDINGS - At the conclusion of debate on H. Res. 1156, the Chair put the question on agreeing to the resolution, and by voice vote, announced that the ayes had prevailed. Mr. Thompson (CA) demanded the yeas and nays and the Chair postponed further proceedings until a time to be announced.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H35000","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule on the resolution and the preamble.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H. Res. 1156.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 6387, H.R. 6398, H.R. 6409 and H. Res. 1156. The resolution provides for consideration of each measure under a closed rule with one hour of general debate on each measure. The resolution also provides one motion to recommit on H.R. 6387, H.R. 6398, and H.R. 6409.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 1174. (consideration: CR H2913-2920; text: CR H2913)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L220","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule H. Res. 1174 passed House.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L210","actionDate":"2026-04-15","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 1174 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 6387, H.R. 6398, H.R. 6409 and H. Res. 1156. The resolution provides for consideration of each measure under a closed rule with one hour of general debate on each measure. The resolution also provides one motion to recommit on H.R. 6387, H.R. 6398, and H.R. 6409.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2026-04-09","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1025","actionDate":"2026-04-09","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Submitted in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/1156","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"S001148","fullName":"Rep. Simpson, Michael K. [R-ID-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ID"},{"bioguideId":"T000478","fullName":"Rep. Tenney, Claudia [R-NY-24]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"B001260","fullName":"Rep. Buchanan, Vern [R-FL-16]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"M001204","fullName":"Rep. Meuser, Daniel [R-PA-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"S001172","fullName":"Rep. Smith, Adrian [R-NE-3]","isOriginalCospons